      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: FOUNDATIONAL UNDERSTANDING OF INEQUALITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Inequality measures the relative distribution of income, wealth, and opportunities across a population, whereas poverty represents absolute deprivation below a basic threshold.",
        "Wealth inequality is significantly more severe and persistent than income inequality due to asset accumulation and inheritance.",
        "The Lorenz Curve graphically demonstrates income distribution, showing the cumulative percentage of income earned by cumulative percentages of the population.",
        "The Gini Coefficient mathematically quantifies inequality, where 0 represents perfect equality and 1 represents absolute inequality.",
        "India's inequality pattern is driven by a combination of economic, social, and institutional factors, requiring targeted policies like inclusive growth and progressive taxation."
      ],
      "id": "gykjluq"
    },
