    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Gini Coefficient values: 0 represents Perfect Equality, while 1 represents Perfect Inequality (100% inequality).",
        "Lorenz Curve deviation: The further the Lorenz Curve bows away from the 45-degree Line of Absolute Equality, the higher the level of inequality.",
        "SSC Distinction: Poverty is an absolute concept measured relative to a poverty line, while Inequality is a relative concept measuring relative income/wealth gaps."
